.TH BETTERX-SECURELOCK 7 better-xsecurelock\-@VERSION@
.SH NAME
better-xsecurelock \- batteries included xsecurelock setup
.SH DESCRIPTION
You are reading the manual page for the
.B better-xsecurelock
package, this package is a set of scripts and wrappers around multiple utilities
to compose xsecurelock and xss-lock into a setup that provides the minimum
experience expected from a screen locker and screen saver for x11 with the top
tier security of xsecurelock.

.SH CONTENTS
.P
The
.B better-xsecurelock
package contains the following programs, the intended user facing ones come with
their own manual page.

.TP
.B lockerd(1)
Main daemon and wrapper over xss-lock(1), it sets up the environment for all the
sub programs by exporting the config file location, sets the x11 screen saver
timeout and cycle as well as the DPMS standby, suspend and off values.

.TP
.B screenlocker
Program launched by xss-lock(1) upon an XServerScreenSaver event, a login
manager event, or an xdg-screensaver(1) lock call, it wraps xsecurelock as well
as manages dim-screen and delaysleep to provide screen dimming and system auto
sleep if the configuration allows.

.TP
.B dim-screen
Program that dims the screen brightness from 255 to 0 step by step, it leverages
blight(1) to do so.

.TP
.B blight(1)
Program to adjust backlight through the /sys/class/backlight/*/brightness
interface.

.TP
.B delaysleep
Program that waits a configurable amount of time before putting the system to
sleep, this is done with the systemact(1) program by default with the "sleep"
action.

.TP
.B saver
Program that provides the screensaver, the screensaver is randomly started from
a list of possible screensavers, 5 different lists are used, while the specific
list is picked randomly from the screenlocker launch the specific saver is
picked randomly from the used list.

.TP
.B screensaverbar
Program that provides the statusbar during the screensaver, the program is just
a tiny shell script and the statusbar is rendered text within the xterm terminal
emulator.

.SH AUTHOR
.EX
eylles                 <ed.ylles1997 at gmail.com>
.EE
.SH HOMEPAGE
.TP
